{
  "_comment": [
    "The matrix of open-kernel model specs: every family x published size we intend",
    "to support. `gen_specs.py` reads this, derives each ModelSpec from the upstream",
    "config.json, validates it against the catalogue, and writes recipes/specs/<slug>.json.",
    "",
    "This file is the source of truth for COVERAGE. It used to be the 15 hand-written",
    "spec JSONs, which made support a function of who last needed a size: qwen3 had 4B",
    "and 8B but not 0.6B or 1.7B, qwen3.5 had 9B and 27B but not 0.8B/2B/4B. Adding a",
    "row here is all it takes; the spec itself is generated.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  slug     file stem for the generated spec (recipes/specs/<slug>.json)",
    "  repo     upstream HF repo whose config.json defines the geometry",
    "  family   the family this MUST derive to. A mismatch is a hard failure, not a",
    "           warning: it means the recipe routing changed and the row is wrong.",
    "  tag      the model_list.json tag this size ships as (coverage is checked",
    "           against the shipped registry, so a model cannot ship unconsidered)",
    "  xclbin   the installed kernel-set directory name, when one exists"
  ],
